course: dictionary
lesson: 1203
title: Buckwheat is not wheat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can mislead you. Buckwheat has «wheat» in its name, so you might think it is a kind of wheat. Check the clues: the dictionary says it is a plant grown for its small, triangle-shaped seeds. When a name seems to give the answer, read the meaning too.
explain: The seeds are cooked like grain or ground into flour, and the flour is used for porridge, pancakes and noodles. «In Brittany une crêpe is a thin, usually sweet pancake, and une galette is a buckwheat pancake, usually savoury, with ham, cheese or egg.» So a galette is a buckwheat pancake, and it is savoury, not sweet.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. Buckwheat is a good example, because the name fits badly and the clues in the sentence fit well.
fact: Buckwheat is a plant grown for its small, triangle-shaped seeds.
fact: The seeds are cooked like grain or ground into flour.
fact: Despite its name, buckwheat is not a kind of wheat.
fact: Buckwheat has no gluten, so people with coeliac disease can eat it.
fact: Buckwheat is used in Japanese soba noodles, French galettes and Ukrainian, Russian and Polish «kasha».
exercise: What is buckwheat? | A type of bread | A kind of wheat with long, thin grains | *A plant grown for its small, triangle-shaped seeds | A sweet sauce for pancakes
exercise: Why can people with coeliac disease often eat buckwheat? | *It has no gluten | It is always sweet | It is a kind of wheat, so it is easy to digest | It is cooked only in noodles
exercise: «In Brittany une galette is a buckwheat pancake, usually savoury, with ham, cheese or egg.» Find and copy one word that means a pancake made from buckwheat. | savoury | egg | *galette | ham
test: Which is a buckwheat dish? | Fish and chips | Roast potatoes | Chocolate cake | *Japanese soba noodles
test: Despite its name, what is buckwheat? | Made of gluten | A kind of rice | A kind of wheat | *Not a kind of wheat
exam: Which statement about buckwheat is true? | It is only used for sweets | It contains gluten, just like wheat | *It has no gluten, so people with coeliac disease can eat it | It is a kind of wheat
